  "Question": "A triangle and a trapezoid are equal in area. They also have the same altitude. If the base of the triangle is \\(18\\) inches, the median of the trapezoid is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(36\\) inches",
    "B": "\\(9\\) inches",
    "C": "\\(18\\) inches",
    "D": "not obtainable from these data",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The median of a trapezoid joins the midpoints of its nonparallel sides. Its length is the average of the two base lengths, so a trapezoid with median length \\(m\\) and altitude \\(h\\) has area \\(mh\\).\n\nLet \\(h>0\\) be the common altitude, measured in inches. The triangle's area is\n\\[\n\\frac12\\cdot18\\cdot h=9h.\n\\]\nSince the trapezoid has the same area, \\(mh=9h\\). Dividing by the positive altitude gives \\(m=9\\). The median is therefore \\(9\\) inches, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
